<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">abdĭcātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		abdĭco, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a renouncing, disowning</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> Jurid. t. t.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hereditatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 6, 31, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">liberorum,</span>”
				<i>disinheriting</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 6, 8, 47</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Quint. 7, 4, 27</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 6, 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 1, 15</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 7,
				45, 46, § 150 al.</span></i>; cf. Dirksen, Versuch., etc.,
			Leipz. 1823, p. 62 sq.—*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Polit. t. t.</b>, <i>a renunciation
				of an office, abdication</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dictaturae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 6,
					16 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
